  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The chain rule differentiates compositions; implicit differentiation handles curves not solved for \\( y \\); and inverse-function derivatives complete the toolkit.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Chain rule &amp; friends",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>\\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}f(g(x))=f'(g(x))\\,g'(x) \\). Differentiate relations implicitly term by term. For inverses, \\( (f^{-1})'(b)=\\dfrac{1}{f'(a)} \\) where \\( f(a)=b \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "figure",
        "figure": {
          "type": "fn",
          "title": "Implicit Curve and Tangent Line",
          "xrange": [
            -6,
            6
          ],
          "yrange": [
            -1,
            8
          ],
          "fns": [
            {
              "fn": "sqrt(max(0, 25 - x^2))",
              "color": "var(--fig-indigo-2)",
              "label": "x² + y² = 25 (y ≥ 0)"
            },
            {
              "fn": "-0.75*x + 6.25",
              "color": "var(--fig-amber)",
              "label": "Tangent at (3,4)"
            }
          ],
          "points": [
            {
              "x": 3,
              "y": 4,
              "label": "P(3,4)"
            },
            {
              "x": 0,
              "y": 5,
              "label": "(0,5)"
            }
          ]
        },
        "caption": {
          "en": "Implicit differentiation of \\( x^2 + y^2 = 25 \\) yields \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = -\\frac{x}{y} \\). At \\( P(3,4) \\), the tangent slope is \\( -\\frac{3}{4} \\), forming tangent line \\( y - 4 = -\\frac{3}{4}(x - 3) \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Chain rule",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f'(g)\\,g' \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Exponential",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}e^{x}=e^{x} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Logarithm",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}\\ln x=\\dfrac1x \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sine",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{d}{dx}\\sin x=\\cos x \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 3.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Differentiate \\( \\sin(x^{2}) \\).</p>\\[ \\frac{d}{dx}\\sin(x^{2})=2x\\cos(x^{2}). \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Implicit differentiation",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find \\(\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\\) for \\(x^2+y^2=25\\) and the equation of the tangent at \\((3,4)\\).</p>\\[2x+2y\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\\;\\Rightarrow\\;\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{x}{y}.\\]<p>At \\((3,4)\\): slope \\(=-\\tfrac{3}{4}\\). Tangent: \\(y-4=-\\tfrac{3}{4}(x-3)\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "⚠ Common traps — Missing chain factor & implicit product rule",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Forgetting the inside derivative:</strong> The derivative of \\( f(g(x)) \\) requires multiplying by \\( g'(x) \\). A classic error is writing \\( \\frac{d}{dx}[\\cos(4x)] = -\\sin(4x) \\) instead of \\( -4\\sin(4x) \\), or omitting the inner derivative on composite powers like \\( (3x - 1)^5 \\).</p><p><strong>Hidden product rule in implicit terms:</strong> When differentiating \\( x^2y \\) or \\( 3xy \\) with respect to \\( x \\), apply the product rule: \\( \\frac{d}{dx}(xy) = (1)y + x\\frac{dy}{dx} \\). Treating \\( y \\) as a constant is the most common error in implicit differentiation FRQs.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0\"><strong>Inverse function derivative argument:</strong> \\( (f^{-1})'(b) = \\dfrac{1}{f'(a)} \\) where \\( f(a) = b \\). The derivative \\( f' \\) is evaluated at the input \\( a \\), not at the output \\( b \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Find \\(\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\arctan(2x)]\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Chain rule with \\(\\dfrac{d}{du}[\\arctan u]=\\dfrac{1}{1+u^2}\\): \\(\\dfrac{2}{1+4x^2}\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Given the curve \\(x^3 + y^3 = 6xy\\) (the Folium of Descartes), find the slope of the tangent line at the point \\((3, 3)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p>Differentiate implicitly with respect to \\(x\\):</p>\\[ 3x^2 + 3y^2 \\frac{dy}{dx} = 6y + 6x\\frac{dy}{dx}. \\]<p>Substitute \\(x = 3\\) and \\(y = 3\\):</p>\\[ 3(9) + 3(9)\\frac{dy}{dx} = 6(3) + 6(3)\\frac{dy}{dx} \\implies 27 + 27\\frac{dy}{dx} = 18 + 18\\frac{dy}{dx}. \\]\\[ 9\\frac{dy}{dx} = -9 \\implies \\frac{dy}{dx} = -1. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
